project OWNER_AWARE_GOVERNANCE:
  version 1
  title "Owner-aware goal and DAG governance"
  description "Adopt GitHub Issue #4 as an independent post-beta workstream. Separate authority to change the project goal or DAG from recommendation override MIG-08. Principal and owner-confirmation values are caller assertions, not authentication. Preserve preview-first mutation, candidate validation, optimistic locking, and safe-write controls. GOV_REQUIREMENTS completed 3p, GOV_AUTHORITY_CONTRACT completed 4p, GOV_DSL_CONTRACT completed 4p, GOV_INTERFACE_CONTRACT completed 4p, GOV_NORMATIVE_EXAMPLES completed 2p, GOV_DESIGN_ACCEPTANCE completed 2p, GOV_SOURCE_MODEL completed 5p, and GOV_AUTHORITY_CORE completed 5p on 2026-07-26, establishing a cumulative workstream-specific velocity sample of 29p/1d. Requirements fix the threat model, scope, defaults, write boundary, and non-goals. Governance semantics version 1 fixes actual-change classification and pre-change authority. Governance source contract version 1 fixes PrincipalId/PrincipalList syntax, Grammar 4 project fields, declared/effective defaults, source-preserving edits, project init/show behavior, unit-migration compatibility, and the digest-bound pre-change snapshot. Governance interface version 1 fixes an optional actor, repeatable accepted-by-owner assertions, operation-level batch confirmation, ProjectResult v3, MutationResult v2 with GovernanceDecision v1, PTGOV-101 under exit 1, and an atomic Grammar 4/CLI Contract 5 cutover. Normative governance examples fix defaults, preview, owner/delegate authority, missing/matching/wrong confirmation, same- and distinct-owner batches, pre-change self-authorization rejection, stale-digest composition, ordinary operations, atomic activation, and direct-edit guidance as one machine-readable acceptance baseline. Cross-cutting design acceptance traces all 10 Issue #4 criteria, all 15 interface invariants, the source and authority/write examples, nine explicit non-goal boundaries, and the implementation handoff with no open findings. Internal target Grammar 4 parsing, declared/effective metadata and source snapshots, formatting, project init/show/set and batch fields, unit-migration preservation, deterministic actual-change scope classification, caller-assertion normalization, pre-change owner/delegate evaluation, mixed-scope decisions, and PTGOV diagnostics are implemented without changing the active Contract 4 package root or CLI. GOV_CLI_PREVIEW completed 4p on 2026-07-27, bringing the cumulative workstream-specific velocity sample to 33p/2d. Internal target governed direct, batch, and advance planning; ProjectResult v3, MutationResult v2, and GovernanceDecision v1 projections; and the complete Contract 5 registry, text/JSON help, and usage recovery are implemented without exposing the active Contract 4 root or CLI. GOV_WRITE_ENFORCEMENT completed 5p on 2026-07-27, bringing the cumulative workstream-specific velocity sample to 38p/2d. Internal target persistence rejects preview, denied, and invalid results before I/O; routes authorized direct, batch, advance, and governed metadata candidates through Grammar 4 candidate validation; retains expected/current digest, symlink, source-identity, atomic replacement, exclusive output, and post-write checks; and rechecks the original source for existing-document out writes. The current new-document import remains outside governance; any future existing-document replacement must use the common classifier and decision boundary. The target remains absent from the active Contract 4 package root and CLI. GOV_GUIDANCE completed 3p on 2026-07-27, bringing the cumulative workstream-specific velocity sample to 41p/2d. The exact generated direct-edit warning is centralized and shared by target project initialization and the target-only Contract 5 editing Guide. Guide, README, and process guidance distinguish caller-asserted pre-change authority from authentication or durable audit and state that direct DSL editing bypasses the tool-mediated check without technical prevention. GOV_ACCEPTANCE completed 4p on 2026-07-27, bringing the cumulative workstream-specific velocity sample to 45p/2d. Grammar 4, ProjectResult v3, MutationResult v2 with GovernanceDecision v1, the Contract 5 registry/help/Guide surface, owner-aware safe-write enforcement, and the isolated installed-package workflow are accepted and active in the repository source and locally built package. The published 0.3.0 artifact remains Contract 4; release version selection, tagging, publication, and dist-tag changes remain outside this plan."
  as_of 2026-07-27
  duration_unit point
  velocity 45p/2d
  finish GOVERNANCE_ACCEPTED

resource DEVELOPERS:
  title "Implementation capacity"
  capacity 2

resource REVIEWERS:
  title "Normative and safety review capacity"
  description "Only one cross-cutting authority or public-contract review runs at a time"
  capacity 1

resource CLI_SURFACE:
  title "CLI, help, and result-schema ownership"
  description "Avoid concurrent changes to the shared command registry, help, and CLI projections"
  capacity 1

resource WRITE_PATH:
  title "Mutation and safe-write ownership"
  description "Avoid concurrent changes to governed mutation classification and write enforcement"
  capacity 1

resource DOC_SURFACE:
  title "Normative and guidance documentation ownership"
  description "Avoid concurrent cross-cutting edits to requirements, specifications, examples, and guidance"
  capacity 1














milestone ACCEPTANCE_INPUT_READY:
  title "Owner-aware governance acceptance input ready"
  state reached

milestone GOVERNANCE_ACCEPTED:
  title "Owner-aware goal and DAG governance accepted"
















task GOV_ACCEPTANCE ACCEPTANCE_INPUT_READY -> GOVERNANCE_ACCEPTED:
  title "Accept owner-aware governance across source and installed package"
  description "Run focused Core, grammar, mutation, CLI, batch, safe-write, help, guide, documentation, self-use, link, package, and installed-workflow tests. Verify Issue #4 defaults, delegation, confirmations, stale-digest behavior, ordinary mutations, direct-edit guidance, and all explicit non-goals."
  duration 4p
  status done
  priority 55
  requires:
    DEVELOPERS 1
    REVIEWERS 1
    CLI_SURFACE 1
    WRITE_PATH 1
    DOC_SURFACE 1
